1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,606
Hi, I'm Rafad Abdul Rasheed. A buyer may

2
00:00:03,606 --> 00:00:07,211
need to review many suppliers, but each application

3
00:00:07,211 --> 00:00:09,915
arrives with different details and documents.

4
00:00:09,915 --> 00:00:13,521
The challenge is to make the process clear

5
00:00:13,521 --> 00:00:17,127
for suppliers, useful for reviewers, and safe for

6
00:00:17,127 --> 00:00:20,732
the buyer. I'll show one application from start

7
00:00:20,732 --> 00:00:23,887
to decision, then a tax identity mismatch.

8
00:00:23,887 --> 00:00:27,493
These are fictional demo profiles. Zoya works for

9
00:00:27,493 --> 00:00:30,197
another buyer company and can only

10
00:00:30,197 --> 00:00:32,000
see that company's cases.

11
00:00:32,000 --> 00:00:38,110
I'll choose Vikram's supplier profile for Apex Components.

12
00:00:38,110 --> 00:00:43,588
This sample profile belongs to Vikram's own company,

13
00:00:43,588 --> 00:00:48,381
Apex Components. He can enter its legal

14
00:00:48,381 --> 00:00:51,120
identity and address here.

15
00:00:51,120 --> 00:00:55,127
Here Vikram enters tax and business registrations.

16
00:00:55,127 --> 00:00:59,706
Zamp checks their format and later compares related

17
00:00:59,706 --> 00:01:03,140
values with the documents he provides.

18
00:01:03,140 --> 00:01:06,650
This section gives the buyer a named contact

19
00:01:06,650 --> 00:01:10,160
and records who can act for the supplier.

20
00:01:10,160 --> 00:01:13,073
The banking details will later be compared with

21
00:01:13,073 --> 00:01:15,621
the uploaded bank proof before payment setup.

22
00:01:15,621 --> 00:01:18,170
Sensitive values are masked in staff views.

23
00:01:18,170 --> 00:01:21,474
Business activity helps the buyer understand what this

24
00:01:21,474 --> 00:01:23,538
supplier provides and which documents

25
00:01:23,538 --> 00:01:25,190
apply to the case.

26
00:01:25,190 --> 00:01:28,672
The checklist adapts to the supplier's business type.

27
00:01:28,672 --> 00:01:32,153
Each document can be previewed, and Zamp shows

28
00:01:32,153 --> 00:01:35,200
what it read before the supplier submits.

29
00:01:35,200 --> 00:01:38,629
This prepared example starts with one OCR misread.

30
00:01:38,629 --> 00:01:42,057
Vikram compares the PAN card preview with Zamp's

31
00:01:42,057 --> 00:01:45,486
reading, corrects it himself, and explains the change.

32
00:01:45,486 --> 00:01:48,914
The original reading and his correction stay on

33
00:01:48,914 --> 00:01:51,486
record. Checks rerun, but a person

34
00:01:51,486 --> 00:01:53,200
still makes the decision.

35
00:01:53,200 --> 00:01:57,625
Vikram reviews the completed details and makes the

36
00:01:57,625 --> 00:02:00,390
required declarations himself before submitting.

37
00:02:00,390 --> 00:02:04,550
On submission, the document checks run and the

38
00:02:04,550 --> 00:02:07,670
supplier gets a reference and status.

39
00:02:07,670 --> 00:02:10,270
These checks prepare the review;

40
00:02:10,270 --> 00:02:13,390
they do not approve the supplier.

41
00:02:13,390 --> 00:02:20,334
Pooja assigns the case to Rajesh, giving the

42
00:02:20,334 --> 00:02:26,410
review a clear owner and recorded handoff.

43
00:02:26,410 --> 00:02:31,482
Rajesh signs in to his assigned queue.

44
00:02:31,482 --> 00:02:37,279
He opens the submitted documents and validation findings.

45
00:02:37,279 --> 00:02:40,902
Zamp brings the evidence together

46
00:02:40,902 --> 00:02:43,800
for a human review.

47
00:02:43,800 --> 00:02:48,605
After confirming nothing blocks approval, Rajesh records the

48
00:02:48,605 --> 00:02:52,810
decision. The reviewer makes the final call.

49
00:02:52,810 --> 00:02:57,181
Vikram sees the approval notice and can open

50
00:02:57,181 --> 00:03:01,552
the decision. He knows onboarding is complete and

51
00:03:01,552 --> 00:03:04,830
no task remains in this application.

52
00:03:04,840 --> 00:03:08,294
Now a second supplier submits a separate case.

53
00:03:08,294 --> 00:03:11,748
A GSTIN carries the business PAN inside it:

54
00:03:11,748 --> 00:03:15,202
characters three through twelve are that ten-character PAN.

55
00:03:15,202 --> 00:03:17,793
Zamp compares it with the form.

56
00:03:17,793 --> 00:03:21,247
They don't match, so approval pauses and the

57
00:03:21,247 --> 00:03:24,701
supplier is asked to check the right entity's

58
00:03:24,701 --> 00:03:26,860
details. These records are synthetic.

59
00:03:26,860 --> 00:03:33,629
The supplier checks the GST certificate, enters the

60
00:03:33,629 --> 00:03:40,398
number that matches the declared PAN, and explains

61
00:03:40,398 --> 00:03:45,475
the change. Zamp keeps the original

62
00:03:45,475 --> 00:03:48,860
request and response together.

63
00:03:48,860 --> 00:03:55,243
The reply does not approve the case.

64
00:03:55,243 --> 00:03:59,802
A person still needs to

65
00:03:59,802 --> 00:04:03,450
review the updated evidence.

66
00:04:03,450 --> 00:04:11,992
The run history preserves the GST mismatch and

67
00:04:11,992 --> 00:04:17,330
the reason approval was held.

68
00:04:17,330 --> 00:04:19,753
A different case has a registry timeout.

69
00:04:19,753 --> 00:04:22,522
That result is unknown, not a supplier failure.

70
00:04:22,522 --> 00:04:24,945
The team can retry; the supplier does

71
00:04:24,945 --> 00:04:26,330
not need to resubmit.

72
00:04:26,330 --> 00:04:30,033
Zamp brings supplier details, documents and review into

73
00:04:30,033 --> 00:04:33,735
one traceable process. It helps teams catch mismatches

74
00:04:33,735 --> 00:04:37,438
early, gives suppliers a clear next step, and

75
00:04:37,438 --> 00:04:40,678
keeps the final decision with a person.

76
00:04:40,678 --> 00:04:44,381
The records and registry results in this demo

77
00:04:44,381 --> 00:04:48,083
are synthetic. In a pilot, we'd measure decision

78
00:04:48,083 --> 00:04:51,786
time and make sure valid suppliers are not

79
00:04:51,786 --> 00:04:55,489
held unnecessarily. Thank you for your time, and

80
00:04:55,489 --> 00:04:57,340
for watching our walkthrough.
